Smoking?

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:14.420
Yes, I'm afraid your brother took the pipe that Mr. Rutherford sent to us and smoked it.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:16.770
That's why your father's so upset.

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:21.140
Dad know the pipe was smoked.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.310
Well, because it turns brown when you smoke it.

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:25.100
Oh.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:29.480
Dad know why he smoked it.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:34.950
Well, because Wally's at the age where boys think it's smart to try smoking.

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:45.410
Of course I do, Beaver.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:49.510
Would you still like me while I was real bad?

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.080
Yes, but why asking me all this?

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.420
No, I can't understand that, boy.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.070
I confronted him with it, and he denied it, point blank.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:08.870
What you gonna do to him, Dad?

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:13.030
Make him stay in his room all weekend, if necessary,

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.970
till he makes up his mind to come to me and admit the whole thing.

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:19.010
The thing I can't understand is his denying it.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:21.030
It's just not like Wally at all.

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:24.720
No, sir, it's like me.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.150
What?

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:33.050
Yes, sir. Well, I smoked the pipe.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:34.900
You, Beaver?

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:39.600
Yes. My friend came over, and I showed it to him.

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:41.800
And he said I shouldn't wait till I was 21.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:48.850
We tried smoking coffee, but that was no good.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:53.030
So he emptied out some ashtrays, and we smoked that.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.350
And we didn't feel too good.

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:56.370
And my friend was Larry.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:58.660
Oh, Beaver.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:20:59.970
Well, that's...

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:04.600
Fine. You not only smoked, but you went right ahead and let me blame your brother for it.

00:21:05.210 --> 00:21:09.810
Gee, Dad, I wouldn't have let you blame him if I didn't know what you were talking about.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:14.600
But you didn't talk about smoking. You just talked about snakes and lizards.

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:20.570
Baby, you know this is a terrible thing you did.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:25.320
Not only smoking, but you lit matches. You've done all the things you've been told not to do.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:29.580
I know, Mom, and I won't ever, never do it again.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:35.360
And you can lock me in my room, and I won't do anything bad again till I'm 21.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:43.090
Beaver, there's just one thing I want to know about this smoking.

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:44.900
Did Larry put you up to it?

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:48.940
No, sir. We put each other up to it.

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.680
I'm glad you said that, at least.

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:55.670
All right, Beaver, you're going to be punished.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:59.140
And I'm going to call Larry's father and see that he knows all about this.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:21:59.980
You boys...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.640
did something that could have had very serious results.

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:04.660
Yes, sir.

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:08.070
Beaver, why in the world would you and Larry want to smoke?

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:14.300
Well, gee, Mom, everybody's always saying how bad it is

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:16.880
and telling kids not to do it.

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:20.860
And I figured if grown-ups said it was so bad,

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.540
there must be something real good about it.

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:27.950
But there wasn't.

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:29.960
I could hardly...

00:22:30.090 --> 00:22:37.350
my stomach down. Well, Beaver, strange as it may seem, as you grow older, you're going to discover

00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:44.050
that quite a lot of things we tell you were bad really are bad. Yeah, Dad, I guess I kind of

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:54.150
found that out. Well, I suppose I'd better go upstairs and apologize to Wally. Tell him I made

00:22:54.150 --> 00:22:56.890
a mistake. Dad?

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:01.600
I think I'd better do that.

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:03.980
Well, I'm the one that got him blamed.

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:05.640
All right, Beaver.

00:23:15.610 --> 00:23:17.650
Can't imagine the beaver smoking that pipe.

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:19.180
Or Larry either, for that matter.

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:21.260
I don't think either one of them would have done it

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:22.220
if they'd been by themselves.

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.260
Well, then why would they do it together?

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:27.660
Well, I guess that's just one of the unwritten rules

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:28.380
of childhood.

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:29.980
No use doing anything.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.180
bad unless there's someone there to admire you for it.

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:39.830
Hey, what are you turning the lights on for?

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:44.620
Well, I just wanted to see if you were still mad at me.

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:50.160
No, I'm not mad at you, but why would you and Larry do a crazy thing like smoking that pipe?

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:55.540
Well, I don't know. It was there, so he smoked it.

00:23:56.140 --> 00:23:59.800
Well, you're always telling me you want to go out for football and stuff when you get in high school.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.140
Don't you know that smoking could wreck you?

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:05.000
Gee, maybe I'm wrecked already,

00:24:05.900 --> 00:24:07.520
because I can only do two push-ups.

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:10.970
No, I don't think so, B, but you better watch it.

00:24:11.460 --> 00:24:13.660
Yeah, but Dad gave you a big balling out.

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:16.450
How come you're not mad at me

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:17.860
for getting you a balling out?

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:21.340
Well, remember last summer

00:24:21.340 --> 00:24:23.620
when Dad was going to work and he had a flat tire?

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:25.340
Yeah.

00:24:26.250 --> 00:24:27.550
Well, I was fixing a box,

00:24:27.570 --> 00:24:29.650
and I forgot to pick up the nails out in the driveway.

00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:35.510
Well, he never found out that I did it, so I kind of figure I had one balling out coming.

00:24:36.360 --> 00:24:43.000
Well, I remember that, but even if you made it up, I'm glad you did,

00:24:43.860 --> 00:24:46.180
because I don't like to go to sleep with people mad at me.

00:24:47.340 --> 00:24:47.740
Yeah.

00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:50.000
Good night, Wally.

00:24:50.360 --> 00:24:50.840
Night, beef.

00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:04.170
Thank you.
